※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4408 LANG_TYPEDEF_CONTAINS_ITSELF

※ An array whose type says its length is its elements, held where the array is:
※ a `Grid⟦2⟧` inside a `Grid` is two of them inside one, without end.  A list
※ would do -- `cells : [Grid]` is where some are and how many -- and so would a
※ reference, but an array is no indirection and is refused (4408) as a field of
※ the type itself would be.

type Grid = cells : Grid⟦2⟧ | empty : void

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    0u6
